preConditionHook:
// THE LITERAL HEAD-AND-SHOULDERS ENTRY: price closes beyond the NECKLINE,
// the line through the two pullback extremes that sit between the shoulders
// and the head. Brooks argues AGAINST this trade ('a breakout below the
// neckline in a bull market will usually fail'), which is exactly why it is
// worth testing as stated -- and testable NEGATED, which is the trade he
// recommends, through the per-placement toggle.
//
// THE PATTERN IS INLINED, not referenced: HeadAndShouldersPattern's peaked
// test, same pivots and same shoulderSymmetryTicks tolerance, per the settled
// composites decision (named Brooks setups keep depends_on_keys in the row
// and inline the parts in code). lookbackBars and shoulderSymmetryTicks are
// promoted to inputs here for that reason; the merged parameters listed only
// swingStrength and entryTick, but the inlined pattern needs both, and they
// carry HeadAndShouldersPattern's defaults so the two files agree at default.
//
// WHICH PIVOTS THE NECKLINE USES. For a TOP the pattern is the three high-side
// pivots -- 1 right shoulder, 2 head, 3 left shoulder -- and the two pullback
// lows BETWEEN them are low-side occurrences 3 (left shoulder to head) and 2 (head
// to right shoulder), occurrence 1 being the low made after the right
// shoulder, which is the one this breakout is heading through. The BOTTOM is
// the mirror: the pattern is the three low-side pivots and the neckline runs
// through high-side occurrences 3 and 2.
//
// THE LINE is TLValue, MEASURED (EL_TLValue_Probe.txt, TLVALUE_FINDINGS.md
// section 4): a pure two-point interpolation anchored at the FIRST pair,
// Slope = (Price2-Price1)/(Bar2-Bar1), value = Price1 + (Target-Bar1)*Slope,
// extrapolating freely past both anchors. The bar convention is the CALLER's;
// bars-ago is used, so the OLDER pivot (the LARGER bars-ago, occurrence 3) is
// passed as Price1/Bar1 -- the zero-drift spelling -- and the target bar is
// 0, the current bar. Bar1 = Bar2 does NOT halt, it silently returns 0.0, so
// both twins guard it explicitly. The slope is hoisted out of the arithmetic
// here where the EL twin recomputes it inside TLValue: identical doubles, so
// bit-for-bit the same line.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS INLINED from ThreePushPattern rather than reaching into
// SwingHigh.json -- rules in this corpus never reference each other, and the
// register lists occurrence 3 as UNMEASURED while occurrence 3 is both the
// left shoulder and a neckline anchor. Measured pivot rule
// (EL_Swing_Probe.txt, @ES 60 min): at-or-beyond the swingStrength OLDER
// bars, STRICTLY beyond the swingStrength NEWER ones (the strict half is the
// k < j loop, el_gt/el_lt, bars-ago making the smaller index the newer bar;
// the at-or-beyond half is the k > j loop, el_ge/el_le); confirmation lag
// exactly swingStrength bars, hence j from swingStrength; candidate offsets
// 0..Length-1 inclusive, so the deepest bar touched is
// lookbackBars - 1 + swingStrength; the comparisons carry the 2.22e-12
// relational tolerance; -1 SENTINEL on prices and bars, every use gated on
// the count reaching 3; the low side's tie sense is the mirror of the
// measured high-side rule. No WFSafe_SwingHigh exists, so plain EL governs,
// and no early break is used -- Break is not a registered EasyLanguage word.
//
// entryTick (Brooks's one tick) is the margin the close must clear the line
// by; the tick is ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale(), division-first, both
// VERIFIED and per-symbol constant for the run.
//
// Scratch below is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope: the
// generator only prefixes declared locals, so a hook-scope declaration is a
// redefinition when this rule is placed twice in one strategy. Every one is
// fully assigned each bar before it is read.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
pivS = (int)swingStrength;
pivW = (int)lookbackBars;
nHiPiv = 0;
nLoPiv = 0;
hiPx1 = -1.0;
hiPx2 = -1.0;
hiPx3 = -1.0;
hiB2 = -1.0;
hiB3 = -1.0;
loPx1 = -1.0;
loPx2 = -1.0;
loPx3 = -1.0;
loB2 = -1.0;
loB3 = -1.0;
for (int j = pivS; j <= pivW - 1; ++j) {
    bool okHi = true;
    bool okLo = true;
    for (int k = j - pivS; k < j; ++k) {
        if (!el_gt(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (int k = j + 1; k <= j + pivS; ++k) {
        if (!el_ge(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && nHiPiv < 3) {
        nHiPiv = nHiPiv + 1;
        if (nHiPiv == 1) hiPx1 = high[j];
        if (nHiPiv == 2) { hiPx2 = high[j]; hiB2 = (double)j; }
        if (nHiPiv == 3) { hiPx3 = high[j]; hiB3 = (double)j; }
    }
    if (okLo && nLoPiv < 3) {
        nLoPiv = nLoPiv + 1;
        if (nLoPiv == 1) loPx1 = low[j];
        if (nLoPiv == 2) { loPx2 = low[j]; loB2 = (double)j; }
        if (nLoPiv == 3) { loPx3 = low[j]; loB3 = (double)j; }
    }
}
hsTop = (nHiPiv == 3) && el_gt(hiPx2, hiPx3) && el_gt(hiPx2, hiPx1) && el_le(std::fabs(hiPx3 - hiPx1), shoulderSymmetryTicks * tickSize);
hsBottom = (nLoPiv == 3) && el_lt(loPx2, loPx3) && el_lt(loPx2, loPx1) && el_le(std::fabs(loPx3 - loPx1), shoulderSymmetryTicks * tickSize);
haveNeckDn = (nLoPiv == 3) && (loB3 != loB2);
haveNeckUp = (nHiPiv == 3) && (hiB3 != hiB2);
neckSlopeDn = 0.0;
neckSlopeUp = 0.0;
if (haveNeckDn) neckSlopeDn = (loPx2 - loPx3) / (loB2 - loB3);
if (haveNeckUp) neckSlopeUp = (hiPx2 - hiPx3) / (hiB2 - hiB3);
neckDn = 0.0;
neckUp = 0.0;
if (haveNeckDn) neckDn = loPx3 + (0.0 - loB3) * neckSlopeDn;
if (haveNeckUp) neckUp = hiPx3 + (0.0 - hiB3) * neckSlopeUp;
